The compilation errors you are seeing are caused by two things:
 1. **Duplicate Code:** You accidentally pasted the workflow initialization block twice inside the same method.
 2. **Type Mismatch:** Your dto.getScheduledTime() is already a LocalDateTime object (because Spring Boot automatically converts it from the frontend JSON), so you cannot use String methods like .isEmpty() or .replace() on it.
Lastly, the executeOraclePostingProcedure error is from the processWorkflowAction method (not this one), because it was a placeholder I put for your existing execution logic.
Here is exactly how to fix all of these issues.
### 1. Fix the createBatchRequest Method
